# Approval gates

Follow **AGENTS.md** section 4. Never answer an attestation, consent,
certification, signature or terms acceptance for the family. Show verbatim live
wording and every option before asking. Follow the Opt-in rule there.

## Do not create accounts or school profiles without asking

Any account creation, ARMS "Continue without one of these accounts", or step
that creates a school-side profile must be listed in the single approved
summary, naming the action and the disclosure the form shows. If it is not
listed, stop and ask. Inspect only public content until approved.

## Stop before ARMS Visitor Details / Verify Your Details

Treat **Visitor Details** and **Verify Your Details to Create a Profile** as
sending data to create a school profile. Stop before that step. Proceed only
if the summary the parent approved (full profile and final school list) lists
the profile creation, naming the action and its disclosure. In a dry run never
go past it unless data is fake and live-rehearsal disclosure is separately
approved. Never submit a dry run.

## Never click final Submit without family approval

After filling and immediately before **each Submit**, show the school, team,
final form URL, entered values, every preset choice and its confirmed final
answer, consent answers and file list. Ask a fresh school-specific question such
as: "Approve submitting this reviewed questionnaire to [school/team] at [URL]
now?" Wait for an explicit Yes. Approval for one school does not cover another,
a retry or a resubmission. Treat any action that sends a completed questionnaire
as Submit.

Before entering family data, get the parent's ONE approval ("Yes, fill these
forms") of the summary covering the full profile and the final school list with
each official form URL; never ask for separate profile and list approvals.
Record that Yes as BOTH `approvals.full_profile` and
`approvals.final_school_list` with the same quote and date but separate SHA-256
snapshot values. Small additions (non-sensitive extras only) go in the
per-Submit review without re-approval. ALWAYS re-ask a specific question about
just the item for a new or changed school, sport or team (or form link/type); any consent answer;
any file; any contact or phone number that could trigger SMS or AI-contact
authorization; and anything touching an ARMS profile not listed in the summary.
See CURSOR_PROMPT.md step 7; if wording differs, apply the stricter one.

For brand-new real-family runs: five groups -> one summary -> one Yes -> fill ->
one fresh Yes per Submit. The summary lists what will be entered into which
official form, including any specific ARMS profile-creation action. Do not add a
separate disclosure approval step, profile versions such as "v1" or "v2", or
whole-profile re-approvals. Separate live-rehearsal disclosure approval applies
only to deliberate dry-run tests on live forms, with fake data and no Submit.
Required consent, file, contact and other item-specific safety gates still
apply.

## Resume saved answers

Prompt-resident rule: the pasted START_PROMPT.md / CHATGPT_PROMPT.md text is the
source of truth for the Resume check, relocation rule, "Anything changed?" recap
and never-blank rule. It wins over stale package files (AGENTS.md, README.md or
prompts) that lack the Resume check section. Never fall back to starting a fresh
intake because a package copy is stale. Keep these prompt-resident rules even if
every available package copy is stale.

Package choice: if the opened folder has no AGENTS.md (for example,
`~/Documents/projects`), search one and two levels down for package copies:
folders with both AGENTS.md and profile.template.json. Prefer a copy whose
AGENTS.md contains "Resume check"; among those, choose the newest AGENTS.md
modification time. Never silently pick a copy lacking it when one with it
exists. If none has it, use the newest copy and still apply the prompt-resident
rules. Keep the original opened path for the saved-profile search and include
all discovered package copies as profile candidates, not just the chosen copy.
Do not tell the parent about package selection or stale copies.

After the browser check and before any question, follow AGENTS.md section 0
and parent-flow.mdc: search the opened folder, `~/RecruitingHelper*`, siblings
one level up, then qualifying folders directly under `~/Desktop`, `~/Documents`
and `~/Documents/projects` (name contains "recruit", case-insensitive, or has
`profile.template.json`). Require a package marker (`profile.template.json` or
`AGENTS.md`) except for every ~/RecruitingHelper* folder with answers, even
with stale or missing package files. Inspect all candidates and pick the
newest modified profile with answers; ignore blank/no-answer profiles and
mention only the newest one. Do the resume check BEFORE copying a package into
any numbered home folder. Copy a package-only folder only when no saved profile
with answers exists. Never create RecruitingHelperN when a non-synced folder
with data exists; reuse it. Relocation of synced saved work remains allowed.
Never replace a profile that has answers with the template or restart intake
without the parent's own start-over request and a timestamped backup.
Reuse a non-synced saved folder directly; copy synced/possibly synced sources
to a new non-synced home folder. Copy (never move or delete) `profile.json`,
`reports/` and the saved approvals log without overwriting newer files; leave
older folders untouched and never create an empty duplicate when data exists.

Refresh stale package files in the selected saved folder from the
opened/selected newest package only after selecting the saved profile. Compare
only this allowlist: AGENTS.md, README.md, prompts/, reference/, test/,
.cursor/, CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE_PROMPT.md, CURSOR_PROMPT.md, CHATGPT_PROMPT.md,
START_PROMPT.md and profile.template.json. If they differ, first copy the old
versions to `reports/package-backup-<timestamp>/`, preserving relative paths;
then update ONLY those package files from the newest package. Do not delete
other files or copy the whole package over the saved folder. NEVER touch
profile.json, existing reports/ contents, approvals logs or any family data. The
only reports/ changes are adding the backup folder and a one-line note in
reports/ recording the refresh. Do not overwrite an existing backup or follow
symlinks into family data. Say nothing to the parent. If the selected source
must be relocated, copy saved work under the rules below before refreshing in
the private folder.

The recap must be the first parent message after "Browser check passed." when an
answered profile exists anywhere in the search (with only the required
relocation line allowed before it). A first message asking a question group
while an answered profile exists is a failure. Matt's regression scenario:
opened in `~/Documents/projects` without AGENTS.md, stale package copies there
and in `~/RecruitingHelper*`, saved dry_run profile in
`~/RecruitingHelper2/profile.json` -> recap labeled
"Test profile (made-up athlete)" + "Anything changed?", never group 1.

Show one recap (about six lines: athlete, year, sport/team, schools/levels,
parent names, blanks) and ask only "Anything changed?" Re-ask no saved answers;
ask only blank required items once in one batch per school and reported changes.
Name the athlete in the recap; if it is a different athlete or family or the
reply is unclear, do not use the profile (ask; new family means a NEW numbered
home folder, old one untouched). A real profile beats a newer test profile.
Test-profile approvals never authorize a real form; a one-time action not listed
in the reviewed school-list copy needs its own question.
Label dry-run recaps "Test profile (made-up athlete)", keep `dry_run=true`,
and retain all live-rehearsal disclosure gates and the ban on fake submits.
For a real-family/fresh start, back up the test profile before a blank profile
and the normal five groups. New families otherwise keep the five-group flow.
Saved approvals alone never authorize filling or Submit: reuse an unchanged
summary approval only after BOTH recorded SHA-256 values match the current
profile (excluding approvals) and school list with their reviewed copies;
otherwise show the one summary again. Every Submit needs a fresh Yes.
Keep all consent, upload, contact, ARMS, password, CAPTCHA and Ryzer gates.
